# Page back control placement

When a page has a back control (chevron/link), place it **inline with the page title** — same row, left of the title. Do not put the back control on a row above or below the title.

## Pattern

Prefer `PageHeader` / `AppPageHeader` with `backTo` or `onBack`:

```tsx
<PageHeader
  title="…"
  backTo="/parent"
  backAriaLabel="Back …"
  action={/* primary actions only */}
/>
```

Or match `DirectoryListChrome` manually:

```tsx
<div className="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2.5 sm:gap-3">
  <Link to="…" aria-label="Back …" className="… rounded-full …">
    <ChevronLeft className="h-5 w-5 …" />
  </Link>
  <h1 className="truncate …">{title}</h1>
</div>
```

## Rules

- Back chevron + title share one horizontal flex row (`items-center`).
- Primary actions (Create, Import, Refresh, etc.) stay on the opposite side of the header, not between back and title.
- Prefer a circular icon button with `ChevronLeft`; no separate “Back” text link in the action slot or stacked under the title.
- Apply this on list child pages, detail/edit/create/import flows, and any new page headers that navigate up.
